WEBVTT

01:12.080 --> 01:13.710
You bastard!

01:14.250 --> 01:15.880
She's not hurt.

01:16.760 --> 01:18.380
She only fainted.

01:20.030 --> 01:22.230
Leave this town.

01:22.230 --> 01:24.300
Who asked you?

01:24.300 --> 01:26.390
Why did you kill Nami?! Answer me!

01:27.170 --> 01:31.400
Those born of Darkness must return
to Darkness. That is the law.

01:31.540 --> 01:33.440
You're the only creatures of darkness!

01:33.440 --> 01:35.740
You saw it yourself.

01:39.140 --> 01:44.450
Tragic though it may be,
reality cannot be denied.

02:04.770 --> 02:07.670
It's like a cheap knock-off.

02:08.440 --> 02:10.910
Even with a brand new train running,

02:10.910 --> 02:14.980
the ghosts of the Great War
throng across the Earth.

02:14.980 --> 02:18.350
Of course, I'm one of those ghosts.

02:18.620 --> 02:19.880
In fact...

02:19.880 --> 02:22.680
I'm accompanied by a band of jesters.

02:24.690 --> 02:27.790
I hate Asia!

02:27.790 --> 02:31.300
That jungle...that sergeant...

02:31.300 --> 02:37.270
Always making fun of me...
He wouldn't even call me by my name!

02:37.270 --> 02:39.530
That's enough, Zero Four.

02:39.870 --> 02:42.200
Let him finish, please.

02:42.470 --> 02:47.070
You should always let people finish what
they're saying. Right, Zero Three?

02:48.180 --> 02:51.080
I'm glad I had strict parents.

02:51.780 --> 02:54.090
Zero One says it's okay.

02:54.090 --> 02:56.020
Go on, Zero Four.

02:56.650 --> 03:00.890
Don't think I don't know, all of you...

03:01.230 --> 03:04.660
You're all mocking me!

03:04.660 --> 03:07.030
But there was one man...

03:07.130 --> 03:11.430
Yes, there was one man who
would stick up for me!

03:12.170 --> 03:15.540
A young priest, Asian fellow...

03:16.170 --> 03:20.800
"That's enough, Sergeant! He has a name!"

03:21.210 --> 03:23.780
That's right, my name!

03:23.780 --> 03:25.650
Uh...Uh?

03:25.650 --> 03:30.050
Oh! My name! What's my name?!

03:32.390 --> 03:34.020
It's so hot...

03:34.790 --> 03:38.460
It's so hot I can't stand it, Zero One!

03:52.580 --> 03:56.580
Tenth Night
The Circus Laughs at Midnight

03:56.580 --> 03:58.980
Otomo Police

03:58.980 --> 03:59.180
Otomo Police

03:58.980 --> 03:59.180
So, that punk was working
with the Skullman!

03:59.180 --> 04:03.620
So, that punk was working
with the Skullman!

04:03.890 --> 04:05.420
Well, that's fine.

04:05.420 --> 04:08.130
We'll round 'em up together
and reap the full bounty!

04:08.130 --> 04:10.200
Ever since the Mayor croaked,

04:10.200 --> 04:13.690
there hasn't been time for freelance work,
what with all the extra patrols!

04:14.300 --> 04:15.970
Where'd Shinjo go?

04:15.970 --> 04:17.630
Who knows?

04:19.870 --> 04:24.070
MIKOGAMI

04:19.870 --> 04:24.070

Shun

04:19.870 --> 04:24.070

Hayato

04:29.150 --> 04:31.820
I'm not sure what your intentions are,

04:31.820 --> 04:35.290
but unless you have a warrant,
that's a serious crime!

04:35.290 --> 04:38.460
Who are you really, anyway?

04:38.460 --> 04:43.420
You mean I never introduced myself?
Here's my card...

04:47.500 --> 04:50.270
The guy's a newspaper journalist, no?

04:50.270 --> 04:52.400
He changed jobs. Now he's a murderer!

04:52.400 --> 04:56.640
In that skirmish last night?
Did someone witness it?

04:58.010 --> 04:59.810
Our police chief...

04:59.810 --> 05:04.810
Gisuke Haniwa, you mean?
The least trustworthy source of all!

05:06.850 --> 05:08.650
I see we think alike.

05:09.350 --> 05:12.380
Then, why don't we work together?

05:20.600 --> 05:22.360
Everything's going perfectly.

05:23.640 --> 05:26.470
We have the support of the
board of executives.

05:26.910 --> 05:29.170
Thank you.

05:29.170 --> 05:32.170
What about the "major shareholder"?

05:34.480 --> 05:37.380
It will all be ironed out any time now.

05:39.450 --> 05:40.850
Don't worry.

05:40.850 --> 05:43.690
I've got you covered, Mr. Future Mayor.

05:43.690 --> 05:45.320
Much obliged.

05:50.060 --> 05:51.460
In Mourning

05:51.460 --> 05:55.070
In Mourning

05:51.460 --> 05:55.070

In the murder of Nami Kisaragi four days ago,

05:55.070 --> 05:55.530
In the murder of Nami Kisaragi four days ago,

05:55.530 --> 06:01.030
Hayato Mikogami, the suspected killer,
remains at large.

06:01.570 --> 06:03.200
Thank you!

06:07.410 --> 06:09.810
This should last him a little while.

06:10.080 --> 06:13.950
Boy, his cigarettes sure are pricey though!

06:15.090 --> 06:18.820
WANTED
Hayato
Mikogami

06:31.940 --> 06:33.100
The False
Blind Spot

06:34.140 --> 06:36.630
You scared me!

06:37.210 --> 06:40.080
Oh, shoot, damn it!

06:41.750 --> 06:43.380
Man...

06:43.380 --> 06:45.040
Thank you!

06:46.820 --> 06:50.410
Oh, thank God! I walked all over!

06:50.860 --> 06:53.480
I thought I'd never find you!

06:54.730 --> 06:58.030
Geez, you're a mess!
How many times did you trip?

06:58.030 --> 07:01.830
You jerk! Who do you think I was
shopping for anyway?!

07:01.830 --> 07:03.400
I know, I know.

07:03.400 --> 07:05.370
C'mon now, this way! Hurry up!

07:06.170 --> 07:09.070
At least carry the bag!

07:09.070 --> 07:10.700
Yeah, yeah...

07:16.580 --> 07:23.020
To absorb the pain myself, and put an
end to this tremendous sadness...

07:23.020 --> 07:24.960
That is my mission.

07:30.030 --> 07:34.090
Tonight, at last, we end it all.

07:35.700 --> 07:37.330
Are you ready?

07:41.170 --> 07:43.040
Guess I'm cornered.

07:51.320 --> 07:53.480
Maybe it's time to head back
down the mountain.

07:53.480 --> 07:56.950
How can you say that?! They'll arrest you
the minute you get down there!

07:56.950 --> 08:02.190
Yeah, but I can't hide up here forever.

08:03.030 --> 08:07.760
Don't worry. If worse comes to worst,
there's always ol' Kuroshio.

08:08.300 --> 08:12.260
I'm no help, am I?

08:14.670 --> 08:18.010
No, I'm grateful to you.

08:18.010 --> 08:21.140
I feel bad for having gotten you
mixed up in all this.

08:23.920 --> 08:26.780
I'm not good enough, am I?

08:27.850 --> 08:30.980
I know I can't compare to Nami.

08:32.020 --> 08:36.630
But if you go back into town...

08:36.630 --> 08:39.490
I'm afraid you'll wind up like Jin!

08:40.430 --> 08:44.370
I don't want that! I don't want to be all alone!

08:46.740 --> 08:50.140
Sorry, I'm being selfish.

08:50.510 --> 08:52.840
Yeah, I know.

08:57.520 --> 09:00.620
Trust me.

09:00.620 --> 09:02.450
It's me, okay?

09:19.570 --> 09:22.010
Tonight is a time for prayer.

09:22.010 --> 09:28.140
Tomorrow, at the holy Advent Festival, please
grace us with your powers, O Priestess!

09:35.390 --> 09:37.350
GOZO
KUROSHIO

09:41.590 --> 09:46.220
I have to go out. Make it quick.

09:46.460 --> 09:50.730
Certainly, I'll get straight to the point.

09:52.100 --> 09:55.600
The time has come for you to
step down as chairman.

10:01.710 --> 10:05.880
Actually, I've decided to go into politics,

10:05.880 --> 10:08.890
and I thought you should leave
the company with me.

10:08.890 --> 10:11.120
I suppose I'm getting old.

10:11.660 --> 10:14.390
They say history repeats itself.

10:14.460 --> 10:17.230
So, it's Masaki.

10:17.230 --> 10:20.200
Well? Is he any good?

10:20.200 --> 10:22.070
Not as good as you.

10:22.070 --> 10:25.740
I don't know if he could have handled the
Kagura Family incident like you did.

10:25.740 --> 10:28.900
Always talking about the past
is a sign of old age.

10:29.240 --> 10:31.640
Well, we can't help aging.

10:31.640 --> 10:37.910
I spent my entire youth doing
thankless tasks for you.

10:38.250 --> 10:41.650
Particularly when you ordered me to get rid of
Mikogami, one of our oldest members,

10:41.650 --> 10:45.950
even if it was to protect the secrecy
of the Gago Project.

10:48.230 --> 10:49.850
Who's there?!

11:24.360 --> 11:28.320
Nice moves! Let's see some more dancing!

11:31.900 --> 11:33.840
Well, look who it is!

11:33.840 --> 11:37.170
Mikogami's son, the murderer!

11:37.170 --> 11:39.300
Your father must be rolling over in his grave!

11:40.780 --> 11:44.080
Mr. Kuroshio, is it true what he said?!

11:55.760 --> 11:57.390
Mr. Kuroshio!

11:59.460 --> 12:01.600
Go, Hayato!

12:01.600 --> 12:04.730
I have nothing left now but my sins!

12:05.170 --> 12:06.800
Sir!

12:07.310 --> 12:08.930
Mr. Kuroshio!

12:12.880 --> 12:16.780
There's still one shot left,
Director Funakoshi.

12:16.780 --> 12:22.520
You should know that there isn't a
single person left on your side.

12:40.300 --> 12:43.330
At least you've got Oscar-worthy bluster!

12:52.950 --> 12:54.580
There!

12:55.020 --> 12:59.890
As suspected, he's working with
two of the Lost Numbers.

13:00.260 --> 13:03.360
Helen says she has visual confirmation.

13:03.360 --> 13:05.490
So what?

13:06.660 --> 13:10.470
It won't go down like the
South Asian War this time!

13:10.470 --> 13:13.560
The words of a man who's never seen war.

13:15.070 --> 13:19.310
Granted, SIRKS is now the most
powerful cyborg squad,

13:19.310 --> 13:22.210
our very latest and best products.

13:22.210 --> 13:27.520
But there are still too many uncertain
elements that could skew the results.

13:45.270 --> 13:46.900
That's nothing!

13:58.520 --> 14:00.140
This is fun!

14:02.120 --> 14:06.690
They're soldiers who were unable to return
to a normal life after the war.

14:06.690 --> 14:10.930
Nameless war dead...
All that's left for them is to fight on.

14:10.930 --> 14:12.930
The trouble is...

14:12.930 --> 14:15.700
...the part that lives on in those dead bodies.

14:15.700 --> 14:20.970
That's the greatest thorn in my side,
and in theirs.

14:39.520 --> 14:44.590
They say that in war, a moment's hesitation
can cost you your life!

14:53.200 --> 14:54.900
What?!

14:55.440 --> 14:57.070
Hayato?

14:59.140 --> 15:00.770
Hayato...

15:04.220 --> 15:07.980
Zero Four, you defective piece of crap!

15:08.190 --> 15:11.490
It's hot! So hot!

15:11.490 --> 15:13.920
It's like a steam bath!

15:15.030 --> 15:18.390
This is why I hate the jungle!

15:28.740 --> 15:30.780
Kiriko Mamiya!

15:30.780 --> 15:32.500
I finally found you!

15:34.080 --> 15:36.750
Where is he?
Where are you hiding him?

15:36.750 --> 15:40.550
He disappeared without telling me!
I'm looking for him too!

15:40.550 --> 15:43.490
What a pathetic lie! Spill it, girlie!

15:43.490 --> 15:44.820
It's the truth!

15:44.820 --> 15:45.820
Now, talk!

15:45.820 --> 15:46.790
Watch out!
Now, talk!

15:49.730 --> 15:51.520
You're a stubborn one!

16:20.460 --> 16:22.580
Boy, that missed us by a hair!

16:23.760 --> 16:26.500
They say that in war, a moment's hesitation
can cost you your life!

16:26.500 --> 16:28.400
Right...

16:28.800 --> 16:32.760
No, Sergeant! They made me...

16:34.670 --> 16:39.200
I know! I can do my job, Sergeant!

16:41.350 --> 16:45.150
C'mon, now! Where are you hiding, kitty-cat?

16:51.860 --> 16:53.360
Mistress Sara!

16:53.360 --> 16:55.290
It's like a war zone outside!

16:55.290 --> 16:56.790
Get a hold of yourself!

16:56.790 --> 16:58.900
Where do you think you are?!

16:58.900 --> 17:00.830
I'm sorry!

17:07.970 --> 17:10.130
Forgive the intrusion.

17:12.780 --> 17:16.510
I'd like to escort my bride to safety.

17:21.890 --> 17:23.510
M-Mother!

17:24.150 --> 17:26.720
H-Hot...Hot...

17:26.720 --> 17:28.630
Don't make fun of me!

17:28.630 --> 17:30.420
I have a name too!

17:31.700 --> 17:35.220
What is my name?

17:35.770 --> 17:37.730
My name...

17:40.270 --> 17:41.840
Whoopsies!

17:41.840 --> 17:45.570
Oh, dear, it's so hard not to kill you!

17:47.480 --> 17:50.310
Almost time for you to go nighty-night!

17:57.820 --> 17:59.450
Tetsuro!

18:01.560 --> 18:03.860
Please carry out your mission.

18:05.600 --> 18:07.220
Hurry!

18:08.270 --> 18:09.890
Forgive me.

18:14.870 --> 18:16.670
Good God...

18:17.070 --> 18:20.480
What the hell's going on?!

18:33.790 --> 18:36.820
No! I can't take it anymore!

18:40.200 --> 18:44.290
I can't get it off! It won't come off!

18:45.740 --> 18:49.930
Please, Sergeant!

18:50.610 --> 18:53.200
I...I...

19:04.820 --> 19:06.690
Save me...

19:06.690 --> 19:10.220
Please save me, Chaplain.

19:10.760 --> 19:15.030
My name! I don't know my name.

19:15.030 --> 19:17.900
Nobody will tell me!

19:23.370 --> 19:25.000
Jack...

19:26.980 --> 19:28.600
It's Jack.

19:30.710 --> 19:33.010
Jack Goodman...

19:33.380 --> 19:36.110
That's your name.

19:46.360 --> 19:48.190
Please wait.

19:49.800 --> 19:56.360
The target has already been removed.
I'm terribly sorry.

19:58.410 --> 20:00.040
And Tetsuro?

20:03.950 --> 20:05.650
I'm sorry.

20:05.650 --> 20:07.880
He had no regrets.

20:08.520 --> 20:10.890
I should know.

20:11.960 --> 20:15.890
He was my only brother after all.

20:31.410 --> 20:32.640
It's you?

20:32.640 --> 20:35.410
Don't talk. It hurts, doesn't it?

20:35.410 --> 20:37.210
I'll get...

20:37.210 --> 20:38.840
Oh!

20:39.150 --> 20:42.020
It's nothing to be sad about.

20:42.020 --> 20:46.480
Now, at last, I am liberated.

20:54.360 --> 20:56.570
What?! What did you say?!

20:56.570 --> 20:59.970
Hey, stay with me! Hey!

21:03.340 --> 21:08.010
Tatta hitotsu no sora shika nai yo

21:08.010 --> 21:12.450
Donna ni sekai ga hirokutatte

21:12.580 --> 21:17.120
Daiji na hito to hagureta toki

21:17.120 --> 21:22.720
Miageru mono ga yuukizukeru

21:22.860 --> 21:27.500
Kyou made aruite kita michi

21:27.500 --> 21:32.000
lma wa futatsu ni wakareteru

21:32.000 --> 21:40.840
Namida wa mata au hi no kokoro no shirushi

21:41.110 --> 21:45.680
Ashita wa ashita no kimi ga umareru yo

21:45.680 --> 21:50.850
Nagai yoru wo koe hi ga noboru you ni

21:50.850 --> 21:54.860
Yume no tsuzuki subete sutete

21:54.860 --> 21:59.120
Ryoute wo hirogeyou

21:59.360 --> 22:04.000
Mirai wa itsudemo kimi no me no mae de

22:04.000 --> 22:09.010
Fumidasu sono toki wo zutto matteiru

22:09.010 --> 22:13.110
Chiheisen no mukou gawa ni

22:13.110 --> 22:20.920
Mada minu sekai tsugi no deai

22:25.220 --> 22:25.660
Eleventh Night


22:25.220 --> 22:25.660
Darkness, Take My Hand

22:25.660 --> 22:28.290
Eleventh Night


22:25.660 --> 22:28.290
Darkness, Take My Hand

22:25.660 --> 22:28.290

The hour of repentence is nigh.

22:28.290 --> 22:31.760
Eleventh Night


22:28.290 --> 22:31.760
Darkness, Take My Hand

22:28.290 --> 22:31.760

Tonight, let loose thy pride.

22:31.760 --> 22:38.370
Eleventh Night


22:31.760 --> 22:38.370
Darkness, Take My Hand

22:31.760 --> 22:38.370
The Mask speaks the truth:
"Rend with me, and forge a covenant."
